meta {
  name: update-settings
  type: http
  seq: 2
}

patch {
  url: {{base_url}}/api/admin/v1/settings
  body: json
  auth: bearer
}

headers {
  Content-Type: application/json
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{access_token}}
}

body:json {
  {
    "tax_bps": 500,
    "service_charge_bps": 0,
    "upi_payee_name": "Spice Garden"
  }
}

tests {
  test("responds 200", function () {
    expect(res.status).to.equal(200)
  })
}

docs {
  # Update settings

Owner/manager only -- floor staff move orders through the kitchen, they do not reprice the menu.

Things worth provoking:

- `"tax_bps": 20000` -> 422. Bounded 0..10000, so a typo'd `5000` cannot charge every diner 50%.
- `"timezone": "Mars/Olympus"` -> 422. Validated on write rather than falling back at read time,
  because an unknown zone would silently roll the daily order counter over at the wrong hour and
  nobody would know why.
- `"payment_provider": "stripe"` -> `TX_PAY_005`. Refused because accepting a provider this
  deployment cannot serve would leave the payment screen quietly falling back on every order while
  the owner believes their gateway is live.

Rate changes apply to **new** orders only; orders already placed keep the rate they were priced at.
}
